{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/crutkas/msys2-runtime/pulls/34","id":4503413730,"node_id":"PR_kwDOT3jXmM8AAAABDGyj4g","html_url":"https://github.com/crutkas/msys2-runtime/pull/34","diff_url":"https://github.com/crutkas/msys2-runtime/pull/34.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/crutkas/msys2-runtime/pull/34.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/crutkas/msys2-runtime/issues/34","number":34,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Guard runtime generation with receipt-last atomic publishing","user":{"login":"crutkas","id":1462282,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0NjIyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1462282?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/crutkas","html_url":"https://github.com/crutkas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/crutkas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/crutkas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/crutkas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/crutkas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/crutkas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/crutkas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/crutkas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/crutkas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/crutkas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":true},"body":"## Summary\n\nApply the qualified three-file runtime generation hardening on an independent branch based exactly on #33 at `563662010c2f2072ad90f28713611caabdf70dbb`. Intended comparison base: `crutkas-arm64-runtime-integration`. This PR does not modify, push, or merge that branch.\n\n- Route the actual TLS, DEF, and signal make targets through an always-run Perl guard. Validate TLS pairing/alignment, source DIN versus generated DEF export equality, real assembly labels, and public providers.\n- Stage generator writes privately, rename each artifact atomically, and publish the hash-bound receipt last. This is per-artifact atomic publication, not a filesystem-wide transaction. Preserve unchanged output timestamps and avoid reassembling `sigfe.o` on a no-op.\n- Close a newly reproduced receipt gap: validate the existing receipt's output set and hashes **before** deciding to regenerate for changed inputs. Corrupt or missing output cannot disappear into an otherwise legitimate rebuild; explicit cleanup must remove the affected receipt before regeneration.\n- Keep `gentls_offsets` unchanged and use only existing Perl core modules in the production guard. Python is used only by the configured-make regression harness.\n\n## Evidence lineage\n\n| Stage | Fresh evidence | Meaning |\n|---|---|---|\n| Sealed proposal | Byte-exact application of patch SHA256 `50736b8ccbdbca6df589a5d514db0d55fc27e698a1fab547dc374a612175dbd7`; all 50 sealed inputs verified; 16 actual-make and 40 existing TLS controls pass | Baseline only; those 16 controls do **not** cover the newly found gap |\n| New adversarial case | Changed `SIGNAL_GENERATOR` plus corrupt `sigfe.s` incorrectly returned exit 0 with the sealed guard | Reproduces stale-input-signature bypass before the successor fix |\n| Successor | 26 actual configured-make controls and 40 existing TLS controls pass | Includes corrupt/missing TLS, DEF, and ASM with changed inputs; preservation of all other artifacts; valid changed-input regeneration and no-op; missing public provider; and clean regeneration |\n\nThe case set directly asserts good TLS SHA256 `49ac682b8f5ed4295d03abc2dab5953fc472684d42eb0b87d779057942b23566`, **1,822 bytes / 59 entries**. The unmodified historical `.long`-only parser, with only its basename output convention adapted, still produces exactly **56 bytes**, SHA256 `95e965fc1beea943c3eadc2cd941c34b01a3151968a0ffbe6917b354d2f0d8a5`; actual make rejects it and preserves the good artifacts. The real historical stale signal generator is also rejected.\n\n## Durable proof\n\nWindows evidence: `C:\\agtc-signal-01\\runtime-generation-application-3fc49c8a`\n\n- `handoff.json`: SHA256 `5fd646b577eec81083f31fe1e532b0387f0e02d509ec457c3f8b1fce306c078b`\n- Sibling 170-file manifest `runtime-generation-application-3fc49c8a.manifest.json`: SHA256 `8fdf475ac76350ed75a791ace5bf9cfefacf52e739b746e3cf41ab0f8f895776`\n- Successor patch: SHA256 `61d1a0b72ad9af6e80288029937de5ae3f415a6d0d18db2f72445a5d894c95a8`\n- Final `make-controls-final-02/result.json`: SHA256 `f045f2b371282247c90748237b1631d0df7bc86bde947ca4545bb4490527aef9`\n\nOwned WSL root: `/root/arm64-vnext-20260905/runtime/atomic-generation-20260911-3fc49c8a`. Source, build, and copied prefix were reconfigured there before any make; the known-good TLS file was backed up first. All host generation/assembly ran serially with at least 8 GiB memory available. No full DLL build, runtime ABI changes, tool installs, main-checkout edits, session67 writes, frozen-root writes, upstream filing, or merges.","created_at":"2026-09-11T07:03:28Z","updated_at":"2026-09-11T07:03:28Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"ec634ee2ace11aebc2b6bc987b062c15aad92805","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/crutkas/msys2-runtime/pulls/34/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/crutkas/msys2-runtime/pulls/34/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/crutkas/msys2-runtime/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/crutkas/msys2-runtime/issues/34/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/crutkas/msys2-runtime/statuses/df7d66f9b1433c50dd7cd234b0d8bd1213418b22","head":{"label":"crutkas:crutkas-atomic-runtime-generation","ref":"crutkas-atomic-runtime-generation","sha":"df7d66f9b1433c50dd7cd234b0d8bd1213418b22","user":{"login":"crutkas","id":1462282,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0NjIyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.git